{
 "name": "VCSL Keys (music-production build)",
 "comment": "Built from the Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL) by Versilian Studios, CC0 1.0. Source: https://github.com/sgossner/VCSL at c1ea7bcc3c7309650ab0da9d15c9cd1fbc4a4c7e. Harpsichords (French 0:6; Flemish 8-foot 1:6 and 8+4-foot 2:6; English lute stop 3:6; velocity sets no level, as on the instrument), a Kawai grand (0:1, four dynamics), two upright pianos (Yamaha 0:3, Knight 1:3) and three Yamaha TX81Z FM voices (FM piano 0:4, piano 1:4, clavinet 0:7). Takes ring until they fall 60 dB under their peak. Changes: pitch-checked against file names, small intonation offsets as fineTune, leading silence trimmed, levels matched per layer, 16-bit TPDF dither; the release samples are not used. Build b2 levels the three acoustic pianos' recorded dynamics and round robins (every dynamic and round robin of a note at one level, on a register slope the dynamics share, each take moved by up to 12 dB), so the velocity curve sets loudness and the layers set the tone. Build b3: on Harpsichord French, Harpsichord Flemish 8, Harpsichord Flemish 8+4, Grand Kawai, Upright Yamaha, Upright Knight, FM Piano TX81Z, FM Piano 1 TX81Z, Clavisynth TX81Z, each half-octave band of a take from 1 kHz up is taken out once it has come down to the recording's hiss, never in the first 0.06 s of a note and never where it would lower the take's peak or level (close_hiss); every other preset is as it was.",
 "copyright": "Source samples CC0 1.0 (Versilian Studios VCSL)",
